Line 2: I can only take items from a list, but this is a number.
    say items 1 to 2 of 5
                        ^

Line 3: The number of items has to be a number, but this is text.
    say the first "two" items in scores
                  ^^^^^

Line 4: The position of an item has to be a number, but this is text.
    say items "a" to 2 of scores
              ^^^

Line 5: I can only take items from a list, but this is text.
    say every second item of "text"
                             ^^^^^^
To take characters of text, write it with "characters", like "characters 2 to 4 of word".

Line 6: I can only take items from a list, but this is a number.
    say 5 without the last item
        ^

Line 8: "words" is a list of numbers (made on line 7), but this is a list of text.
    set words to a list of "x"
                   ^^^^^^^^^^^
A variable keeps the kind of value it was made with. To keep a list of text, make a new variable for it.
